=======================================
FORMAL ONTOLOGICAL DEFINITION OF THE POINT
=======================================

Axiom 0 — Locationless Primitive (Non-Locality)
---------------------------------------
∄ (coordinates, embedding, metric, substrate) ∈ P

The Point P cannot be assigned a location in any pre-existing geometry, as it precedes geometry.

Axiom 1 — Generative Primitive (Generativity)
---------------------------------------
P : ∅ → R        (R = relational structure)

The Point is a generator of relational fields, not an operator on them.

Axiom 2 — Relational Collapse (Minimal Stance)
---------------------------------------
P = argmin_{s ∈ S} |{ s : ∀ ¬s ∈ S, s ⊨ ¬s }|

The Point is the minimal stance that survives all counter-relations.

Axiom 3 — Counter-Structural Stability (Survivability)
---------------------------------------
P = { p | p ⊨ ∃ ¬p  ∧  p ⊨ ¬(¬p ⊨ ¬p) }

A Point is what remains after its negation fails to negate it.